boot [meas: CtrlTest boot]: loader 23 words + hello 36 code + 2 data words = 16 128-bit mode-6 packets (spec 6.2) and 2 command writes (mode 7) from C&C; all 64 READY at cycle 56, RUN raised at 56, every tile at main's ebreak by 139
registers [meas: CtrlTest registers]: write-only reads 0; counters 20 bits, writes add and wrap (flagged); HIST 17, PTR 21, the STREAM arrays and GROUP 32 bits a word through the window; send port modes 2, 6, 7, 8 to the tile itself at 32, 64 and 128 bits with auto-increment +1/+2/+4 (mode 6) and +1 (mode 7), W0-W2 cleared per send; counters done after each; the wake registers' resets; status and done readable the next cycle
command phases [meas: CtrlTest commands]: per GO, all-READY -> GO store (C&C) and READY round trip
  GO 0: all READY at 239, GO stored at 240, seen by tiles at 241-242
  GO 1: all READY at 282, GO stored at 283, seen by tiles at 284-285
  GO 2: all READY at 324, GO stored at 325, seen by tiles at 326-327
  GO 3: all READY at 366, GO stored at 367, seen by tiles at 368-369
  GO 4: all READY at 932, GO stored at 933, seen by tiles at 934-935
  two-command phase: start store 28 cycles after GO on every tile; local copy of 512 records, start -> READY 535 cycles
  the next command, sent right after GO: its first mailbox write lands 6 cycles after the tile saw GO at the earliest (tile 0), into the other argument block;
  its slot 0 (zero-argument commands) 6 cycles after GO at the earliest, after the woken tile read the previous command word (the simulator checks every slot-0 landing)
WFI [meas: CtrlTest wfi]: counters done before WFI falls through in 1 cycle and wfi()'s load returns it; done clears it; GO is sticky (a WFI after a missed GO falls through); READY fires at done when the command landed first; uncounted packets made 256 counters-done edges that the qualifier kept from setting it
faults [meas: CtrlTest faults]: store to TILE_STATUS, load from instruction memory, sub-word register store, the table window's gap and a misaligned load are bus errors; div and a CSR read are illegal; ecall halts; each cause logged, its condition set, no READY; HALT clears the conditions and HALT -> RUN restarts every core at the loader
invariants [meas: CtrlTest invariants]: 4 (done before arrivals), 5 (a mode-0 packet sent), 7 (packet in flight at a line change), 8 (reply overwritten unread), 9 (unexpected arrival: its condition set; a store to the reserved MASTER_PULSE[3] ignored and flagged; M14) and the table-window check each fire on a bad program
block copy [meas: CtrlTest block copy]: 1,024 words (256 128-bit mode-6 packets) big SRAM -> instruction memory by the 6.5 sequence, from the start store to the first instruction after WFI: 271 cycles (spec 4.2: about 256 plus the stream's start; v1.0's 512 64-bit packets took 527)
